 "title": "A 2² experiment: the interaction plot",
 "caption": "A has main effect (14 + 20 − 10 − 12)/2 = 6 and B has 4. The lines for B− and B+ are not parallel: A raises the response by 4 when B is low but by 8 when B is high, so the interaction is (10 + 20 − 14 − 12)/2 = 2.",
 "alt": "Two lines against the level of A (−1 and +1): B− from 10 to 14 and B+ from 12 to 20, the second steeper.",
 "description": [
  "At B−, moving A from − to + raises the response from 10 to 14.",
  "At B+, it raises it from 12 to 20.",
  "Different slopes mean an interaction: 2."
 ],
